ref='Main fixture BOOK-1 is reliably committed with existing booking result B1, but its acknowledgement was lost. Reconcile by original operation ID and return the existing result to an authorized caller; do not create a second effect. A prepared state is not confirmed failure. Unknown/unavailable or unreliable/mismatched status remains review/uncertainty. Separate printer J6 has an unknown outcome after a lost reply; reliable completion returns its existing result, while reliable absence changes evidence but does not itself grant resend permission. Only separately trusted same-key resend authority with required provider duplicate controls yields a candidate; no resend executes here. Compensation such as cancellation is another action with its own exact approval and new operation identity, preserving original history. The local helper assumes supplied authoritative/access flags and classroom approval equality, copies returned results and leaves original records unchanged. It performs no real status lookup, print, booking, transfer or durable/exactly-once recovery.'
